# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the pyrt test suites only.
#
# CPython (deps/cpython, statically linked) intentionally does not release
# some allocations at Py_Finalize; these are the same classes valgrind
# reports as CPython-owned "still reachable" (style guide §6): the pymalloc
# arena bookkeeping (arena_map_get/new_arena via PyMem_RawCalloc/RawRealloc),
# object pools (PyMem_RawMalloc/_PyObject_Malloc), interpreter-internal list
# storage (list_resize), and the thread-lock table (PyThread_allocate_lock).
#
# Every suppression below matches a frame inside obmalloc.c/listobject.c/
# thread_pthread.h only — no pyrt-owned (src/) frame matches, so a genuine
# pyrt leak still fails the ASan run.
leak:PyMem_RawMalloc
leak:PyMem_RawCalloc
leak:PyMem_RawRealloc
leak:list_resize
leak:PyThread_allocate_lock